From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:38:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: compute the swap_pace floor cap in 64
 bits

The cap on the learned swap_pace floor multiplies the counter frequency
by 600 us. arch_timer_get_cntfrq() returns u32, so the product is taken
in 32 bits and wraps: on the J604 the counter runs at 1 GHz, and the
cap came out at about 3 us instead of 600 us. No swap's start-to-
completion time is that short, so the learner never took a value since
the cap was added, and swap_pace has used its 350 us fallback lead on
every boot (debugfs pace lead_us read 0 on 1.730 and 1.732).

The fallback lies inside the range of leads that land held frames on
their aim, so no cadence was lost (held swaps missing their tick 0.5 %
on 1.730), but the floor was meant to be learned. Widen to 64 bits
before the multiplication.

Fixes: 5830213ab844 ("drm/apple: m4: do not take a swap_pace floor above 600 us")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit 37e24a6640b9238816ae8c8c3f99f9a342ed1d54)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index e37b56fe50..f8c0a4838a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1861,7 +1861,7 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	if (prev && start < prev + div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 120))
 		return;
 	lat = done - start;
-	max = div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq() * DCP_M4_PACE_LEAD_MAX_US, USEC_PER_SEC);
+	max = div_u64((u64)arch_timer_get_cntfrq() * DCP_M4_PACE_LEAD_MAX_US, USEC_PER_SEC);
 	if (!r->int_lat_n || lat < r->int_lat_win)
 		r->int_lat_win = lat;
 	if (lat <= max && (!READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) || lat < READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min)))
-- 
